{
  "prompt": "Hand-drawn sketches in pencil on aged paper, illustrating abstract physics concepts. One sketch shows curved filaments (like tangled strings or braids) wrapping around an empty central space. Another sketch shows angled planes labeled 'Zeit' (German for time) slicing through these filaments, creating intersection points. One of the points is marked with a question mark. The style is messy, energetic, with cross-outs and handwritten German notes in the margins. The overall feeling is that of a young scientist exploring complex ideas through raw, intuitive drawings.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A hand-drawn, slightly rough sketch by a 17-year-old Albert Einstein in 1896. The drawing shows a poetic map of a landscape, not precise, but evocative: winding lines representing footpaths, soft branching patterns like river deltas or neural networks, clusters of dots for villages, and swirling shapes where 'the land remembers'—places of historical passage. The style is youthful, a little chaotic, with visible pencil pressure variations, on yellowed, creased paper. It feels more like a web of experiences than a geographical map.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A hand-drawn notebook sketch from 1896, in the style of a young Albert Einstein. The sketch shows a metaphorical diagram titled 'Information fährt nicht — es faltet'. The drawing includes wavy filaments ('Zotten') twisting and looping, with arrows indicating how information moves by modulating the relation between points, not by moving material directly. Small annotations in German handwriting explain concepts like 'Spannung' (tension), 'Faltung' (folding), and 'Beharrlichkeit' (persistence). The style is mechanical, intuitive, with simple but precise lines, resembling an old physics student's notebook.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A hand-drawn notebook sketch from 1896, in black ink, by a 17-year-old Albert Einstein. The sketch shows a simple figure labeled 'Ich' (me) standing under a giant, heavy stone monument labeled 'EINSTEIN' in big block letters. But instead of looking serious, the small figure sticks out its tongue playfully. Around the figure are scribbled notes in German handwriting: 'Fragen, Stolpern, Spielen' (asking, stumbling, playing) and 'Kein Denkmal, nur ein Mensch' (not a monument, just a person). The style is youthful, messy but clever, with arrows and small doodles illustrating the weight of expectations versus personal curiosity.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A hand-drawn style pencil sketch, aged like a notebook from 1896. The drawing shows a young man named Bellomy standing over a broken mechanical device — wires, gears, and tensioned springs burst apart mid-motion. A teacher points at the mess, mid-phrase saying 'You broke it, Bellomy' — not angrily, but with weary inevitability. Bellomy looks surprised, but also curious, almost proud. In the background, other students are frozen mid-glance. Above the scene is a faint handwritten title: 'Where systems reveal their seams.' The sketch should have a thoughtful, metaphorical tone, like an early Einstein or Feynman notebook.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A hand-drawn sketch in black pencil on aged notebook paper, made by a 17-year-old Albert Einstein in 1896. The sketch shows a symbolic 'Time Braider': a human figure at the center, with several twisted strands of time radiating outward, some like spirals, some like ropes or light beams. The strands connect to small symbols—an old train, a car, a moon, a pocket watch, a telescope, and a device like a glowing rectangle (representing a modern smartphone). The style is mechanical and intuitive, like an early scientific notebook with notes scribbled in a mix of German and English. The page is smudged, slightly worn, and full of curiosity.",
  "size": "1024x1024"
}

{
  "prompt": "A futuristic highway scene inspired by the user's photo, showing a wide American interstate under a partly cloudy sky. The highway is flanked by green trees and sound barriers. Overhead is a large digital sign with glowing blue and red interstate shields (e.g., I-71, I-70, I-270) and green text displaying estimated travel times. The car interior and dashboard are partially visible in the foreground. The setting is mid-21st century but grounded in realistic design.",
